# Fixed result-grid column widths for DBeaver.
#
# Copy this file to your home directory as   dbeaver-widths.properties
#   Linux / macOS : ~/dbeaver-widths.properties
#   Windows       : C:\Users\<you>\dbeaver-widths.properties
# (or point the patch elsewhere with -Ddbeaver.widths.file=... in dbeaver.ini)
#
#   key    = column header text as shown in the grid, case-insensitive
#   value  = width in pixels, a bare integer - no "px"
#   *      = fallback for every column without an entry of its own
#
# The file is read as UTF-8 and reloaded whenever it changes:
# save it, press F5 on the grid, done. No restart.
#
# TRAP: a space inside a column name MUST be escaped with a backslash.
# The .properties format ends the key at the first unescaped space, so
#   Value Space Value2=140   is read as key "Company", value "Name=140"  -> ignored
#   Value\ Space\ Value2=140  is correct
# Parentheses, dots and digits need no escaping. Only spaces.
#
# Errors here are silent: a bad value just means that column keeps the width
# DBeaver computed for it.

# Default for anything not listed below. Comment it out to leave unlisted
# columns to DBeaver's own calculation.

Example\ Value=110